BT 1 0 0 1 0 35.7 Tm /F1 8.3 Tf 11 TL (The application will maintain a shared record of inventory and the complete order lifecycle. Customers will browse products, submit) Tj T* (orders, view shipment status, cancel eligible quantities, and request returns. Warehouse employees will receive inventory, work) Tj T* (through picking queues, record dispatches, and inspect returns. Managers will oversee stock levels, fulfillment delays, and activity) Tj T* (across all warehouses.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 60 326 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 24.7 Tm /F1 8.3 Tf 11 TL (When an order is placed, the system will check available quantities and reserve stock within a database transaction. It will first try to) Tj T* (fulfill the order from one warehouse; if that is not possible, it will split fulfillment using a documented stock-based allocation rule. An) Tj T* (order that cannot be fully reserved will be rejected without leaving partial reservations. Payment and carrier updates will be simulated.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 60 288 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 24.7 Tm /F1 8.3 Tf 11 TL (Before shipment, cancellation will release the corresponding reservation. After shipment, an approved return will enter inspection; only) Tj T* (quantities accepted as resalable will be added back to available stock. Each role will have enforced access rules: customers access) Tj T* (their own orders, warehouse employees access assigned warehouse work, and managers access cross-warehouse reports.) Tj T* ET
